Subject: Cantor Identity Accounting Journal and Host Protocol P1 Requirement Matrix

& [RequirementMatrix]
  + IAJ-01 valid exact genesis is verified by genesis_is_deterministic_replayable_and_canonically_restorable
  + IAJ-02 deterministic contiguous events are verified by equal genesis and patch executions plus sequence assertions
  + IAJ-03 semantic patch replay is verified by patch_appends_one_semantically_replayable_generation_and_preserves_history
  + IAJ-04 closed snapshots and events are verified by missing snapshot refusal and complete retained-set validation
  + IAJ-05 stale journal compare-and-set refusal is verified after a successful successor
  + IAJ-06 inert reads are verified by project resolve inspect read-ledger and read-event transitions with no successor
  + IAJ-07 complete projection or refusal is verified by three-member window and one-byte capacity refusal
  + IAJ-08 explicit resolved ambiguous and unknown outcomes are verified without fuzzy selection
  + IAJ-09 exact object ledger and event reads are verified with unknown event refusal
  + IAJ-10 P0 patch compare-and-set is verified by successful patch plus stale object version refusal
  + IAJ-11 append-only preservation is verified by two retained ledgers and two retained events after one patch
  + IAJ-12 exact response binding is verified by request substitution refusal and operation-result recomputation
  + IAJ-13 canonical bounded persistence is verified by byte-identical encoding restore and insufficient-bound refusal
  + IAJ-14 strict machine form and tamper refusal is verified by unknown-field whitespace missing-snapshot digest and semantic validation
  + IAJ-15 pure core boundary is verified by module inspection and absence of clock filesystem provider network and effect calls
